ic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_PinchView":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_pinchview","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pinch to scale a shape. A "},{"code":"MagnifyGesture","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (Origami’s magnification\/pinch input)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drives two "},{"code":"origami.PopSwitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" nodes that flip the shape between its base and an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"enlarged state; the switch state feeds a "},{"code":"builtin.point3D","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" Transform Scale, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the pop is animated with a spring. At rest a white rounded triangle sits at base"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scale, centered on the magenta artboard."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_PinchView"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_PinchView"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_PinchView","title":"Interaction_PinchView","kind":"symbol"}}}